IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-core`
IMPORT `sg-periods`
IMPORT `sg-definitions`
IMPORT `sg-interpretation`

-- Companies Act 1967 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, SSO informal consolidation "version in force from 6/5/2026 to 20/10/2026":
-- s 216, "Personal remedies in cases of oppression or injustice" (LAYER 1: the law, objectively; part sgf).
--
-- What is here: who may apply to the Court (s 216(1) and (7)); the two grounds (s 216(1)(a), (b)); the Court's power to make an
-- order and each of the six powers the order may include (s 216(2)(a) to (f)); the winding-up consequence (s 216(3)); the bar on
-- further alterations to the constitution and the effect of the alterations the order makes (s 216(4)); the duty to lodge a copy of
-- the order in 14 days and the offence of not doing so (s 216(5), (6)); the regulative rules for the duty and the bar.
--
-- How a result reads. JUST TRUE: the text says yes. JUST FALSE: the text says no in its own words. NOTHING: the text does not say.
-- A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE. Every branch that answers no or not-covered carries the kind of its answer in a comment.
-- Judgments the text hands to someone else (the Court's opinion that a ground is established, whether conduct is oppressive,
-- whether a person is a member) are plain inputs, named for the fact.
-- The Minister's limb (a declared company under Part 9) and the Court's powers are encoded for what they mean to the individual;
-- there is no seat for either.

§ `Section 216(1): who may apply, and the two grounds`

-- (1) lead: "Any member or holder of a debenture of a company or, in the case of a declared company under Part 9, the Minister,
-- may apply to the Court for an order under this section on the ground". A function named for a grant ("may apply"): where the
-- applicant is outside the class the text names (a body that is not a company, a person who is none of the three, a court that is
-- not the Court) the answer is NOTHING (the grant ruling of 2026-11-12, limit 1; fork F-216-1 in NOTES.md).
-- "Declared company under Part 9" is a term of another part: asked as a fact.
-- src:21700 | 216.—(1) Any member or holder of a debenture of a company or, in
-- src:21701 | the case of a declared company under Part 9, the Minister, may apply
-- src:21702 | to the Court for an order under this section on the ground —
@ref s 216(1) (src:21700-21702)
GIVEN `the body is a company incorporated under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the body is a company incorporated under a corresponding previous written law` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a member of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `shares in the company have been transmitted to the person by operation of law` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a holder of a debenture of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the Minister` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company is a declared company under Part 9` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court applied to is the General Division of the High Court` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 216(1) the person may apply to the Court for an order under this section` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 4(1) "Court" the court is the Court` `the court applied to is the General Division of the High Court` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may apply to the Court" -- the grant is of an application to the Court, which s 4(1) defines as the General Division of the High Court
        IF    ((`s 216(7) the person is treated as a member for the purposes of the section` `the person is a member of the company` `shares in the company have been transmitted to the person by operation of law` EQUALS JUST TRUE) OR `the person is a holder of a debenture of the company`)
          AND (`s 4(1) "company" the body is a company` `the body is a company incorporated under this Act` `the body is a company incorporated under a corresponding previous written law` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the person is the Minister` AND `the company is a declared company under Part 9`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Any member or holder of a debenture of a company or, in the case of a declared company under Part 9, the Minister, may apply" -- the grant names a member or holder of debentures of "a company" (s 4(1): one incorporated under the Act or a corresponding previous written law) and the Minister of a declared company, without "only"; a person or a body outside those is outside the limit

-- (1)(a): the first ground. The conduct is (i) the affairs of the company being conducted, or (ii) the powers of the directors being
-- exercised; the manner is (A) oppressive to one or more of the members or holders of debentures (including the applicant), or
-- (B) in disregard of their interests as members, shareholders or holders of debentures. Whether the matter complained of is within
-- "the affairs of the company" is s 4(8) (which names s 216) and s 4(9): the list is open ("including"), so a matter off it is
-- NOTHING, never FALSE. Whether the manner is oppressive, or in disregard of interests, is the Court's kind of judgment: a plain input.
-- A contrary intention under s 4(8) (fork F-216-2): none is read in s 216, so FALSE is passed.
-- src:21704 | (a) that the affairs of the company are being conducted or the
-- src:21705 | powers of the directors are being exercised in a manner
-- src:21706 | oppressive to one or more of the members or holders of
-- src:21707 | debentures including the applicant or in disregard of his,
-- src:21708 | her or their interests as members, shareholders or holders
-- src:21709 | of debentures of the company; or
@ref s 216(1)(a) (src:21704-21709)
GIVEN matter IS A `s 4(8) matter`
      `the corporation is a trustee and is not a trustee corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the act or thing was done at a time when a receiver, or a receiver and manager, was in possession of or had control over property of the corporation, the corporation was under judicial management, a compromise or an arrangement between the corporation and another person was being administered, or the corporation was being wound up` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the corporation has issued interests` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the powers of the directors are being exercised in the manner complained of` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the manner complained of is oppressive to one or more of the members or holders of debentures, including the applicant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the manner complained of is in disregard of the interests of one or more of the members, shareholders or holders of debentures as such` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 216(1)(a) the ground is established` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT (`the manner complained of is oppressive to one or more of the members or holders of debentures, including the applicant` OR `the manner complained of is in disregard of the interests of one or more of the members, shareholders or holders of debentures as such`))
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "on the ground (a) that the affairs of the company are being conducted or the powers of the directors are being exercised in a manner oppressive ... or in disregard of ..." (the provision's own question: neither manner is present)
        IF `the powers of the directors are being exercised in the manner complained of`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `s 4(8) a reference to the affairs of a corporation covers the matter` TRUE FALSE matter `the corporation is a trustee and is not a trustee corporation` `the act or thing was done at a time when a receiver, or a receiver and manager, was in possession of or had control over property of the corporation, the corporation was under judicial management, a compromise or an arrangement between the corporation and another person was being administered, or the corporation was being wound up` `the corporation has issued interests` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): s 4(8) says the affairs of a corporation are "to be construed as including" the listed matters; a matter off the list may still be the affairs of the company, and the directors' powers are not being exercised

-- (1)(b): the second ground. An act of the company done or threatened, or a resolution of the members, holders of debentures or a class
-- of them passed or proposed, which unfairly discriminates against, or is otherwise prejudicial to, one or more of the members or
-- holders of debentures (including the applicant).
-- src:21711 | (b) that some act of the company has been done or is
-- src:21712 | threatened or that some resolution of the members,
-- src:21713 | holders of debentures or any class of them has been
-- src:21714 | passed or is proposed which unfairly discriminates against
-- src:21715 | or is otherwise prejudicial to one or more of the members
-- src:21716 | or holders of debentures (including the applicant).
@ref s 216(1)(b) (src:21711-21716)
GIVEN `an act of the company has been done or is threatened` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a resolution of the members, holders of debentures or a class of them has been passed or is proposed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the act or resolution unfairly discriminates against one or more of the members or holders of debentures, including the applicant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the act or resolution is otherwise prejudicial to one or more of the members or holders of debentures, including the applicant` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 216(1)(b) the ground is established` MEANS
    IF    (`an act of the company has been done or is threatened` OR `a resolution of the members, holders of debentures or a class of them has been passed or is proposed`)
      AND (`the act or resolution unfairly discriminates against one or more of the members or holders of debentures, including the applicant` OR `the act or resolution is otherwise prejudicial to one or more of the members or holders of debentures, including the applicant`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "on the ground (b) that some act of the company has been done or is threatened or that some resolution ... has been passed or is proposed which unfairly discriminates against or is otherwise prejudicial to" (the provision's own question: an element is unmet)

-- (1) read with (2): "either of such grounds". Takes the two answers above.
-- src:21700 | 216.—(1) Any member or holder of a debenture of a company or, in
-- src:21701 | the case of a declared company under Part 9, the Minister, may apply
-- src:21702 | to the Court for an order under this section on the ground —
-- src:21704 | (a) that the affairs of the company are being conducted or the
-- src:21705 | powers of the directors are being exercised in a manner
-- src:21706 | oppressive to one or more of the members or holders of
-- src:21707 | debentures including the applicant or in disregard of his,
-- src:21708 | her or their interests as members, shareholders or holders
-- src:21709 | of debentures of the company; or
-- src:21711 | (b) that some act of the company has been done or is
-- src:21712 | threatened or that some resolution of the members,
-- src:21713 | holders of debentures or any class of them has been
-- src:21714 | passed or is proposed which unfairly discriminates against
-- src:21715 | or is otherwise prejudicial to one or more of the members
-- src:21716 | or holders of debentures (including the applicant).
@ref s 216(1) (src:21700-21716)
GIVEN `the answer for the ground in paragraph (a)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the answer for the ground in paragraph (b)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 216(1) either of the grounds is established` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the answer for the ground in paragraph (a)` EQUALS JUST TRUE OR `the answer for the ground in paragraph (b)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the answer for the ground in paragraph (a)` EQUALS JUST FALSE AND `the answer for the ground in paragraph (b)` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "on the ground (a) ...; or (b) ..." -- both paragraphs answered no
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): one paragraph answered NOTHING (the matter may still be the affairs of the company), and the other did not establish a ground

§ `Section 216(2): the Court's order, and what it may include`

-- (2) lead: "If on such application the Court is of the opinion that either of such grounds is established the Court may, with a view
-- to bringing to an end or remedying the matters complained of, make such order as it thinks fit". A function named for a power
-- ("the Court may"): where the "if" gate fails, or the order is not made with that view, the answer is NOTHING (the grant ruling of
-- 2026-11-12, limit 1; fork F-216-3). The Court's opinion is a judgment handed to the Court: an input.
-- src:21721 | (2) If on such application the Court is of the opinion that either of
-- src:21722 | such grounds is established the Court may, with a view to bringing to
-- src:21723 | an end or remedying the matters complained of, make such order as it
-- src:21724 | thinks fit and, without limiting the foregoing, the order may —
@ref s 216(2) (src:21721-21724)
GIVEN `the Court is of the opinion, on an application under section 216(1), that either of the grounds is established` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the order is made with a view to bringing to an end or remedying the matters complained of` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 216(2) the Court may make the order it thinks fit` MEANS
    IF    `the Court is of the opinion, on an application under section 216(1), that either of the grounds is established`
      AND `the order is made with a view to bringing to an end or remedying the matters complained of`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If on such application the Court is of the opinion that either of such grounds is established the Court may, with a view to bringing to an end or remedying the matters complained of, make such order as it thinks fit" -- a grant whose "if" gate or purpose is not met; the text does not say the Court may not

-- (2)(a): "direct or prohibit any act or cancel or vary any transaction or resolution".
-- src:21726 | (a) direct or prohibit any act or cancel or vary any transaction
-- src:21727 | or resolution;
@ref s 216(2)(a) (src:21726-21727)
GIVEN `the Court is of the opinion, on an application under section 216(1), that either of the grounds is established` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the order is made with a view to bringing to an end or remedying the matters complained of` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 216(2)(a) the order may direct or prohibit any act or cancel or vary any transaction or resolution` MEANS
    `s 216(2) the Court may make the order it thinks fit` `the Court is of the opinion, on an application under section 216(1), that either of the grounds is established` `the order is made with a view to bringing to an end or remedying the matters complained of`

-- (2)(b): "regulate the conduct of the affairs of the company in future".
-- src:21729 | (b) regulate the conduct of the affairs of the company in future;
@ref s 216(2)(b) (src:21729-21729)
GIVEN `the Court is of the opinion, on an application under section 216(1), that either of the grounds is established` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the order is made with a view to bringing to an end or remedying the matters complained of` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 216(2)(b) the order may regulate the conduct of the affairs of the company in future` MEANS
    `s 216(2) the Court may make the order it thinks fit` `the Court is of the opinion, on an application under section 216(1), that either of the grounds is established` `the order is made with a view to bringing to an end or remedying the matters complained of`

-- (2)(c): "authorise civil proceedings to be brought in the name of or on behalf of the company by such person or persons and on such
-- terms as the Court may direct". The separate route of s 216A (permission for a derivative action) is in sgf-s216a.l4.
