      `the order is made with a view to bringing to an end or remedying the matters complained of` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 216(2)(c) the order may authorise civil proceedings to be brought in the name of or on behalf of the company` MEANS
    `s 216(2) the Court may make the order it thinks fit` `the Court is of the opinion, on an application under section 216(1), that either of the grounds is established` `the order is made with a view to bringing to an end or remedying the matters complained of`

-- (2)(d): "provide for the purchase of the shares or debentures of the company by other members or holders of debentures of the
-- company or by the company itself". The buyer is one of the two the text names or some other person (not listed, not excluded).
DECLARE `s 216(2)(d) buyer` IS ONE OF
    `s 216(2)(d) another member or holder of debentures of the company`
    `s 216(2)(d) the company itself`
    `s 216(2)(d) some other person`

-- src:21735 | (d) provide for the purchase of the shares or debentures of the
-- src:21736 | company by other members or holders of debentures of the
-- src:21737 | company or by the company itself;
@ref s 216(2)(d) (src:21735-21737)
GIVEN `the Court is of the opinion, on an application under section 216(1), that either of the grounds is established` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the order is made with a view to bringing to an end or remedying the matters complained of` IS A BOOLEAN
      buyer IS A `s 216(2)(d) buyer`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 216(2)(d) the order may provide for the purchase of the shares or debentures of the company by the buyer` MEANS
    IF `s 216(2) the Court may make the order it thinks fit` `the Court is of the opinion, on an application under section 216(1), that either of the grounds is established` `the order is made with a view to bringing to an end or remedying the matters complained of` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN (CONSIDER buyer
          WHEN `s 216(2)(d) another member or holder of debentures of the company` THEN JUST TRUE
          WHEN `s 216(2)(d) the company itself` THEN JUST TRUE
          OTHERWISE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "by other members or holders of debentures of the company or by the company itself" names two buyers without "only"; the general power "such order as it thinks fit" is not cut down by the list ("without limiting the foregoing")
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the "if" gate or the purpose of s 216(2) is not met, so the grant is not made out

-- (2)(e): "in the case of a purchase of shares by the company provide for a reduction accordingly of the company's capital".
-- A scope limit with no "only": outside a purchase of shares by the company the answer is NOTHING (periods ruling of 2026-11-05, (c)).
-- src:21739 | (e) in the case of a purchase of shares by the company provide
-- src:21740 | for a reduction accordingly of the company’s capital; or
@ref s 216(2)(e) (src:21739-21740)
GIVEN `the Court is of the opinion, on an application under section 216(1), that either of the grounds is established` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the order is made with a view to bringing to an end or remedying the matters complained of` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the order provides for a purchase of shares by the company itself` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 216(2)(e) the order may provide for a reduction accordingly of the company's capital` MEANS
    IF    `s 216(2) the Court may make the order it thinks fit` `the Court is of the opinion, on an application under section 216(1), that either of the grounds is established` `the order is made with a view to bringing to an end or remedying the matters complained of` EQUALS JUST TRUE
      AND `the order provides for a purchase of shares by the company itself`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in the case of a purchase of shares by the company" -- a scope limit with no "only"; outside it, or without the s 216(2) gate, the text does not say

-- (2)(f): "provide that the company be wound up".
-- src:21742 | (f) provide that the company be wound up.
@ref s 216(2)(f) (src:21742-21742)
