§ `Section 216(3): a winding-up order made under subsection (2)(f)`

-- (3): "Where an order that the company be wound up is made pursuant to subsection (2)(f), the provisions of the Insolvency,
-- Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018 relating to the winding up of a company apply, with such adaptations as are necessary, as if
-- the order had been made upon an application duly made to the Court by the company." A "where" condition on a rule of application
-- (not a grant): when it fails the answer is JUST FALSE (periods ruling of 2026-11-05, (b)). Which winding-up provisions then apply,
-- and how they are adapted, are the other Act's: not encoded.
-- src:21744 | (3) Where an order that the company be wound up is made pursuant
-- src:21745 | to subsection (2)(f), the provisions of the Insolvency, Restructuring
-- src:21746 | and Dissolution Act 2018 relating to the winding up of a company
-- src:21747 | apply, with such adaptations as are necessary, as if the order had been
-- src:21748 | made upon an application duly made to the Court by the company.
@ref s 216(3) (src:21744-21748)
GIVEN `an order that the company be wound up has been made pursuant to subsection (2)(f)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 216(3) the winding up provisions of the Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018 apply as if the order had been made on an application by the company` MEANS
    IF `an order that the company be wound up has been made pursuant to subsection (2)(f)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where an order that the company be wound up is made pursuant to subsection (2)(f), the provisions ... apply ... as if the order had been made upon an application duly made to the Court by the company" -- a "where" condition on a rule of application (periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (b); fork F-216-4)

§ `Section 216(4): the constitution after an order that alters it`

-- (4), first limb: the bar. "Where an order under this section makes any alteration in or addition to any company's constitution, then,
-- despite anything in any other provision of this Act, but subject to the provisions of the order, the company concerned does not
-- have power, without the permission of the Court, to make any further alteration in or addition to the constitution inconsistent
-- with the provisions of the order". A flat negative ("does not have power"): named as the bar, because a bar's NOTHING and FALSE are
-- not a grant. Where no order altered the constitution ("where") the answer is JUST FALSE (periods ruling (b)); where the further
-- alteration is not inconsistent with the order, or the Court has given permission ("without"), the case is outside the limit the
-- bar sets for itself and the answer is NOTHING (forks F-216-5, F-216-6).
-- src:21752 | (4) Where an order under this section makes any alteration in or
-- src:21753 | addition to any company’s constitution, then, despite anything in any
-- src:21754 | other provision of this Act, but subject to the provisions of the order,
-- src:21755 | the company concerned does not have power, without the permission
-- src:21756 | of the Court, to make any further alteration in or addition to the
-- src:21757 | constitution inconsistent with the provisions of the order; but subject
@ref s 216(4) (src:21752-21757)
GIVEN `an order under section 216 has made an alteration in or addition to the company's constitution` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the further alteration or addition is inconsistent with the provisions of the order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court has given permission for the further alteration or addition` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 216(4) the subsection bars the company from making the further alteration or addition to the constitution` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `an order under section 216 has made an alteration in or addition to the company's constitution`)
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where an order under this section makes any alteration in or addition to any company's constitution, then ... the company concerned does not have power" -- the bar is introduced by "where" and no such order has been made (periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (b))
        IF (NOT `the further alteration or addition is inconsistent with the provisions of the order`)
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "to make any further alteration in or addition to the constitution inconsistent with the provisions of the order" -- a scope limit with no "only"; a consistent alteration is outside it
        IF `the Court has given permission for the further alteration or addition`
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "does not have power, without the permission of the Court" -- with the Court's permission the case is outside the limit the bar sets for itself
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- (4), second limb: "but subject to the foregoing provisions of this subsection the alterations or additions made by the order are
-- of the same effect as if duly made by resolution of the company". No alteration made by the order: the text is silent.
-- src:21757 | constitution inconsistent with the provisions of the order; but subject
-- src:21758 | to the foregoing provisions of this subsection the alterations or
-- src:21759 | additions made by the order are of the same effect as if duly made by
-- src:21760 | resolution of the company.
@ref s 216(4) (src:21757-21760)
GIVEN `an order under section 216 has made an alteration in or addition to the company's constitution` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 216(4) the alterations or additions made by the order have the same effect as if duly made by resolution of the company` MEANS
    IF `an order under section 216 has made an alteration in or addition to the company's constitution`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection speaks of "the alterations or additions made by the order"; where the order made none it says nothing about effect

§ `Section 216(5) and (6): lodging a copy of the order, and the offence`

-- (5): "A copy of any order made under this section must be lodged by the applicant with the Registrar within 14 days after the making
-- of the order." Counting: "within 14 days after" is counted by sg-periods.l4 (P1: the day of the order is not counted; P2: an act on any
-- day up to the last day is in time, an early act included). Fork F-216-7 names the other reading (the strict "within a period after").
-- src:21769 | (5) A copy of any order made under this section must be lodged by
-- src:21770 | the applicant with the Registrar within 14 days after the making of the
-- src:21771 | order.
@ref s 216(5) (src:21769-21771)
GIVEN `the date the order was made` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 216(5) the last day for lodging a copy of the order with the Registrar` MEANS
    `period: the last day of a period after` `the date the order was made` 14 Days

-- (5): has the applicant failed to comply? The applicant failed if the copy was lodged after the last day, or has not been lodged and
-- the last day has passed on the day asked. A person who is not the applicant is not the one the subsection binds: JUST FALSE.
-- src:21769 | (5) A copy of any order made under this section must be lodged by
-- src:21770 | the applicant with the Registrar within 14 days after the making of the
-- src:21771 | order.
@ref s 216(5) (src:21769-21771)
GIVEN `the person is the applicant for the order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the order was made` IS A DATE
      `the copy of the order has been lodged with the Registrar` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the copy was lodged` IS A DATE
      `the date on which the question is asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 216(5) the applicant has failed to comply with subsection (5)` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the person is the applicant for the order`)
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must be lodged by the applicant" -- the duty is the applicant's; this person is not the applicant (the provision's own question)
        IF `the copy of the order has been lodged with the Registrar`
        THEN (IF `period: the date is not later than the end of a period after` `the date the order was made` `the date the copy was lodged` 14 Days
              THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must be lodged ... within 14 days after the making of the order" -- the copy was lodged in time, so the duty was met
              ELSE JUST TRUE)
        IF `period: the date is not later than the end of a period after` `the date the order was made` `the date on which the question is asked` 14 Days
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must be lodged ... within 14 days after the making of the order" -- the 14 days have not yet run out, so the applicant has not yet failed
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- (6): "Any person who fails to comply with subsection (5) shall be guilty of an offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine not
-- exceeding $1,000 and also to a default penalty." The default penalty is s 408's (another part): its amount is not here.
-- An unmet element of an offence: JUST FALSE, the provision's own question (split site (i), fork F-216-8).
DECLARE `s 216(6) penalty` HAS
    `the highest fine, in Singapore dollars` IS A NUMBER
    `a default penalty also applies` IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:21773 | (6) Any person who fails to comply with subsection (5) shall be
-- src:21774 | guilty of an offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine not
-- src:21775 | exceeding $1,000 and also to a default penalty.
@ref s 216(6) (src:21773-21775)
GIVEN `the person is the applicant for the order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the order was made` IS A DATE
      `the copy of the order has been lodged with the Registrar` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the copy was lodged` IS A DATE
      `the date on which the question is asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 216(6) the person is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` MEANS
    IF `s 216(5) the applicant has failed to comply with subsection (5)` `the person is the applicant for the order` `the date the order was made` `the copy of the order has been lodged with the Registrar` `the date the copy was lodged` `the date on which the question is asked` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Any person who fails to comply with subsection (5) shall be guilty of an offence" -- an element is unmet (the person has not failed to comply with subsection (5)), so this subsection makes the person guilty of nothing on these facts; it does not say the person is innocent of any other offence (split site (i), fork F-216-8)

-- src:21773 | (6) Any person who fails to comply with subsection (5) shall be
-- src:21774 | guilty of an offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine not
-- src:21775 | exceeding $1,000 and also to a default penalty.
@ref s 216(6) (src:21773-21775)
GIVEN `the person is the applicant for the order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the order was made` IS A DATE
      `the copy of the order has been lodged with the Registrar` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the copy was lodged` IS A DATE
      `the date on which the question is asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 216(6) penalty`
`s 216(6) the most the person may be sentenced to on conviction` MEANS
    IF `s 216(6) the person is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` `the person is the applicant for the order` `the date the order was made` `the copy of the order has been lodged with the Registrar` `the date the copy was lodged` `the date on which the question is asked` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST (`s 216(6) penalty` OF 1000, TRUE)
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection states a penalty only for the person it makes guilty

§ `Section 216(7): a person to whom shares have been transmitted by operation of law`

-- (7): "This section applies to a person who is not a member of a company but to whom shares in the company have been transmitted by
-- operation of law as it applies to members of a company; and references to a member or members are to be construed accordingly."
-- Where the person is a member, the subsection is not needed and the person is a member; for a person who is not a member, the
-- subsection extends the section to the transmittee. For anyone else the subsection says nothing: NOTHING, not FALSE (fork F-216-9).
-- src:21777 | (7) This section applies to a person who is not a member of a
-- src:21778 | company but to whom shares in the company have been transmitted
-- src:21779 | by operation of law as it applies to members of a company; and
-- src:21780 | references to a member or members are to be construed accordingly.
@ref s 216(7) (src:21777-21780)
GIVEN `the person is a member of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `shares in the company have been transmitted to the person by operation of law` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 216(7) the person is treated as a member for the purposes of the section` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the person is a member of the company`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `shares in the company have been transmitted to the person by operation of law`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection extends the section to a person to whom shares have been transmitted by operation of law and says nothing of anyone else

§ `Regulative rules: the duty to lodge (s 216(5)) and the bar on further alterations (s 216(4))`

-- s 216(5) as a rule with a party, an act and a deadline. Time 0 is the day the order is made; WITHIN 14 counts days, and the act is in
-- time on day 14 (the deadline is inclusive) and out of time on day 15. The party is the applicant: a Member, a holder of a
-- debenture (a Creditor), or the Minister: passed in as a Party. Failing to comply is the offence of s 216(6) (the BECAUSE says so).
DECLARE `s 216(5) act` IS ONE OF
    `s 216(5) lodge a copy of the order with the Registrar`

-- src:21769 | (5) A copy of any order made under this section must be lodged by
-- src:21770 | the applicant with the Registrar within 14 days after the making of the
-- src:21771 | order.
@ref s 216(5) (src:21769-21771)
GIVEN applicant IS A Party
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 216(5) act`
`s 216(5) the applicant must lodge a copy of the order with the Registrar within 14 days` MEANS
    PARTY applicant
    MUST `s 216(5) lodge a copy of the order with the Registrar`
    WITHIN 14
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY applicant BECAUSE "a copy of the order was not lodged with the Registrar within 14 days after the making of the order (s 216(5)); failing to comply with s 216(5) is an offence under s 216(6)"

-- s 216(4) as a prohibition, derived from the flat negative "does not have power" (N2, ruled 2026-11-04: where the text names the
-- bearer, the prohibition is derived). The bearer is "the company concerned". The act the company may not do is a further alteration
-- inconsistent with the order WITHOUT the Court's permission; the same alteration WITH permission is a second act that the rule
-- does not forbid. There is no deadline: a company that never does the act has not breached it (the trace reads RESIDUAL).
DECLARE `s 216(4) act` IS ONE OF
    `s 216(4) make a further alteration or addition to the constitution inconsistent with the order, without the permission of the Court`
    `s 216(4) make a further alteration or addition to the constitution inconsistent with the order, with the permission of the Court`

-- src:21752 | (4) Where an order under this section makes any alteration in or
-- src:21753 | addition to any company’s constitution, then, despite anything in any
-- src:21754 | other provision of this Act, but subject to the provisions of the order,
-- src:21755 | the company concerned does not have power, without the permission
-- src:21756 | of the Court, to make any further alteration in or addition to the
-- src:21757 | constitution inconsistent with the provisions of the order; but subject
-- src:21758 | to the foregoing provisions of this subsection the alterations or
-- src:21759 | additions made by the order are of the same effect as if duly made by
-- src:21760 | resolution of the company.
@ref s 216(4) (src:21752-21760)
GIVEN `the name of the company` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 216(4) act`
`s 216(4) the company must not make a further alteration to the constitution inconsistent with the order without the permission of the Court` MEANS
    PARTY Company `the name of the company`
    SHANT `s 216(4) make a further alteration or addition to the constitution inconsistent with the order, without the permission of the Court`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company `the name of the company` BECAUSE "the company made a further alteration in or addition to its constitution inconsistent with the order, without the permission of the Court (s 216(4))"
